Z||000000||Ferrari355||05-07-2000||08:00 PM||||Hey, ok i told you about switching the V6 out of the 86 GT into the 8 4 SE which is a 4banger with auto and the<B>GT</B> a manual. Well i was wondering about the wiring harness will the 86 fit on the 84. <P>     Ok, we tried to take the Fastback off today but something is caught. i took the headliner down and got the 3 out there, my dad took the gas lid off, the bolt under the tailights and the ones that are in the inside. Do we need to take the sail panels off or not? Well let me know, you can e-mail me at   <A HREF="mailto:BKS854@aol.com">BKS854@aol.com</A>   <p>[This message has been edited by Ferrari355 (edited 05-07-2000).]||||reg||4
Z||000001||Jay||05-08-2000||10:27 PM||||If memory serves me correctly, all the harnesses for the V6's are the same with the exception of an 88.  The only difference will be what options the car has such as A/C.  That goes for the four bangers also.  The other thing to watch out for would be if the tranny is staying with each engine.  If an automatic harness is going onto a 4 or 5 speed then some modifications will need to be made.  And DON'T FORGET TO CHANGE THE COMPUTER!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!! Mark them with a black marker so you don't mix them up!!!  Trust me, I've had that happen and it's not fun!||||reg||1
